 "response": "Tido's budget is now **$3,930K**.\n\n**How it was worked out**\n\n- **Whose records count.** Only Finance Office budget entries were used. Notes from the PMO, Vendor, Legal and other teams were ignored. Finance Office entries that don't change the budget were also ignored. These include audits, receipts, purchase orders, room moves and cost-center codes.\n- **Withdrawals.** Every withdrawal chain was resolved from its last link back to the start. If a withdrawal was itself withdrawn, the update it targeted came back into effect. Examples:\n  - #0011 is cancelled by #0031. That leaves #0011 in force, so #0007 (+$303K) stays withdrawn.\n  - #0013 is cancelled by #0091, and #0091 by #0365. #0472 then cancels #0365, which puts #0091 back in force. So #0013 stays cancelled and #0008 (+$209K) stands.\n  - #0011 \u2192 #0031 \u2192 #0175 \u2192 #0575: #0575 is the last link and cancels #0175. That restores #0031, which cancels #0011, so #0007 (+$303K) stands.\n  - #0093 \u2192 #0295 \u2192 #0361 \u2192 #0727 \u2192 #0955: #0955 is the last link. Working back, #0093 ends up in force, so #0028 (+$423K) is withdrawn.\n  - #0120 \u2192 #0130 \u2192 #0145 \u2192 #0237 \u2192 #0268 \u2192 #0831: #0831 is the last link. Working back, #0120 ends up cancelled, so #0041 (\u2212$158K) stands.\n- **Totalling.** Starting from the $1,650K set in #0001, each remaining increase or decrease was applied once, in record order.\n\nANSWER: $3930K",
